{
  "schema": "vitana.delivery-cutover-shards/v1",
  "$comment": "Which parallel CI job runs each test of delivery-cutover.test.mjs (the file takes ~315 s serially). Keyed by exact test name; a shard job throws when a test has no entry. Rebalance with the measured durations (LPT) when tests change.",
  "shards": 4,
  "assignment": {
    "structure: both scripts are strict bash, have no xtrace, name the management account, and reach the world only through the x_ wrappers and W": 1,
    "usage: no command, an unknown command and extra words are exit 2 with the usage; --help is exit 0; nothing is called": 4,
    "status: with every item true it prints the 15 items of plan §8.1 one by one, green, says the cut may start, exits 0, and only reads": 3,
    "status --item: each red condition turns exactly its own item red, names the reason, makes the exit code 1; the other items of the same group stay as they were": 3,
    "status --item: a green item is green and exits 0, an unknown item is a usage mistake, and the full status marks exactly the broken item when two items are broken": 4,
    "status: when git cannot fetch origin/main, the four lane items fail by name and the others still run": 2,
    "preflight: the wrong AWS account, a missing tool, a GitHub token GitHub does not accept and one without admin rights each stop the command before anything is read or changed": 1,
    "the GitHub token is typed hidden when GH_TOKEN is not set, and it appears in no output, no argument and no file": 3,
    "apply: without the plan slug, or with --dry-run, it is a dry run: it shows every change as WOULD, makes none, and still reads the checklist": 2,
    "apply: a wrong plan slug, an unknown option, a real run without --mirror-account and a mirror account that cannot push are refused before anything is changed": 3,
    "apply: with a red checklist it refuses, names the red item, and changes nothing": 1,
    "apply: the cut, step by step in the order of plan §8.2, each change printed before it is made, and every effect in place at the end": 2,
    "apply: step 7 stops when DELIVERY_MODE of a project is not live after the sync, and no tag is made": 1,
    "apply: step 2 does not run the GitHub-to-GitLab copy when the cutover marker is already set (it would overwrite GitLab main with GitHub main)": 2,
    "apply: run again after the cut it does nothing: every step says already done, no state-changing call is made, exit 0": 4,
    "apply: waits for the owner at step 6 (exit 3), is resumed from step 6 when the switch is on, and a switch that is flipped during the wait lets one run finish": 3,
    "failure at step 1: the protection of the first repository is put back, the cut stops, and the next run (after the fix) finishes with the original protection still saved": 1,
    "failure at step 2: a final copy that fails leaves the copy running and changes nothing else; at step 3: a sync that does not converge removes the marker again": 2,
    "failure at step 4: the workflows disabled in that step are enabled again, the cut stops, and the next run disables exactly the list": 2,
    "failure at step 8: the tags made in that step are deleted again on both hosts": 1,
    "rollback: it reverses the cut in the order of plan §8.4, restores exactly what the cut changed, loses no commit, and prints every change first": 4,
    "rollback: it enables again only the workflows the cut disabled; one that was already disabled before the cut stays disabled": 2,
    "rollback: a staging gateway that still carries the cut settings is redeployed through the GitHub path; without the slug or with --dry-run nothing is changed": 4,
    "rollback: it refuses while GitHub main is not GitLab main, and while branches exist only on GitLab, and restores nothing then": 2,
    "rollback: from a cut that stopped half way (the settings sync failed at step 3) it undoes what exists and skips the rest; a second rollback is harmless": 3,
    "rehearse: it needs --merges-paused, opens with the marker \"rehearsal\", waits (exit 3) until a live pipeline on main deployed and verified each repository, then closes and sends staging back to the GitHub path": 1,
    "rehearse --dry-run: opening, closing and aborting print every change as WOULD, make none, and claim no result": 4,
    "rehearse: a red checklist blocks it, --abort closes an open rehearsal without a pass, and an aborted rehearsal is not a pass": 1,
    "machine scripts: every script sent to the GitLab machine starts with its read or write line, parses in plain sh, and names a token file only to test it or to feed it to curl through stdin": 4,
    "machine scripts, run for real in sh on stand-ins: the converge script writes and removes the marker and runs the two syncs; the unit script touches only the named units; the tag script feeds its token to curl through stdin": 3,
    "runbook: every bash block parses, it explains every checklist item, shows the commands of the scripts and states the counts of the workflow list": 1,
    "pipeline runbooks: after the cut tag of a repository the merge bot lands and the driver waits for delivery.landed instead of merging; before the tag the merge flow is unchanged": 1,
    "B1: a backup write that Secrets Manager refuses, or one that reads back different, stops step 1 before that GitHub main is changed": 4,
    "B1: the record of a started cut, and the list of step 4, are read back too: a write that fails stops apply before the change they protect": 3,
    "B1: a 502 on the protection GET stops step 1 and saves nothing; only GitHub's 404 \"Branch not protected\" counts as no protection, and it is restored by a DELETE": 3,
    "B1: a rollback whose protection backup is deleted or cannot be read exits 1 with the manual instruction, never says done, and leaves GitHub main locked": 4,
    "B1: when step 1 cannot put a protection back it says NOT undone, never \"undone\"": 4,
    "B1: rollback step 4 without its saved list exits 1 with the manual instruction while workflows of the disable list are disabled; an unreadable list stops it too": 3,
    "B2: a second rollback after a good one restores no protection and enables no workflow, even when the team changed both since; only disabled_manually workflows of the list are enabled": 4,
    "B2: the rollback records rolling-back before its first change; apply refuses to resume such a cut; the next rollback continues and finishes it": 3,
    "B2: apply resumes a started cut only within 24 hours; an older record needs the checklist green again; the saved protection is kept; another mirror account is refused": 2,
    "B2: a lock keeps runs apart: apply, rehearse and the rollback refuse while it exists; --break-lock clears only a lock older than 6 hours; a run releases its lock": 1,
    "B3: the restore body carries bypass allowances and dismissal restrictions, sends a null app_id as -1, and gives checks or contexts, never both": 1,
    "B3: a cut and its rollback restore a protection with bypass allowances and an any-app check through the documented schema, exactly": 1,
    "B3: rehearse first runs the round trip of the protection (PUT the restore body back, GET, compare) before the marker; the checklist item is green only on the protection of today": 1,
    "B4: the rollback refuses while a branch on both hosts has GitLab commits that GitHub lacks, lists it and restores nothing; a GitLab head that GitHub contains is fine": 2,
    "B4: the bot refs train/* and assist/* are left out of the GitLab-only check; a full 30th page of GitLab branches stops the rollback instead of being cut short": 1,
    "B4: on the machine the GitLab branch listing prints every head, stops at a short page, and says truncated when page 30 is still full": 1,
    "B5: the rollback waits for the redeploy, reads the staging task definition again, and stops with the owner command while DELIVERY_HOST_* is still gitlab": 4,
    "B5: closing the rehearsal waits for both staging redeploys and checks the gateway; with DELIVERY_HOST_* still gitlab the rehearsal stays open and the owner command is printed": 2
  }
}
